Need fix all occurrences in battle.js: `this.addParticles(...this.pos(X), color, count)` -> `const {x,y}=this.pos(X); this.addParticles(x,y,color,count)`. Many. Could create helper method `burst(unit,color,count)` and replace. Simpler: change `addParticles` signature? Could make `addParticles` accept either (x,y,color,count) or ({x,y},color,count)? But calls are spread. If we redefine `this.pos` to return an iterable array [x,y], then `...this.pos()` would work, but other calls `const {x,y}=this.pos(target)` would break (destructuring object from array gives undefined x/y? Actually arrays have no x/y properties, so breaks). Could make pos return an object with Symbol.iterator yielding x,y AND x/y properties. That's clever and minimal:
```
pos(unit) {
  const p = {...};
  return Object.assign(p, { [Symbol.iterator]: function*(){ yield p.x; yield p.y; } });
}
```
